# Start with your first trace

Tracify connects the model calls, tool calls, prompts, costs, failures, and evaluation signals inside an agent run. This guide gets one useful trace into the dashboard.

## Install the SDK

```bash
npm install tracify-sdk
```

Create a project in Tracify and copy its API key. Keep the key in a server-side environment variable:

```bash
TRACIFY_API_KEY=tracify_sk_live_...
```

## Wrap one run

```ts
import { traceAgent } from "tracify-sdk";

const runAgent = traceAgent(
  async (question: string) => callModel(question),
  { apiKey: process.env.TRACIFY_API_KEY },
);

await runAgent(question);
```

## Verify the result

Open the project dashboard and select the newest run. A healthy first trace has a root run, a child span, timing, and the model response. Add `environment`, `release`, and prompt version attributes as you expand the integration.

Next, choose the runtime guide for the [TypeScript SDK](/docs/typescript) or [Python SDK](/docs/python).
